{"schemaVersion":1,"storyId":"poem-harmattan-morning","version":1,"title":"Harmattan Morning (a poem)","ageTiers":["5-6","7-8"],"language":"en","narrationLocale":"en-GH","pages":[{"n":1,"text":"The harmattan wind blows soft and dry.\nIt paints a pale haze across the sky.","sentences":["The harmattan wind blows soft and dry.","It paints a pale haze across the sky."],"alt":"A pale dusty sky over a village at dawn.","image":{"hash":"sha256:92644c78c8c2b617a28655a6e6fe362862aa60992b3b5b1a8002cbc5f064a6b9","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:6a85c07447d7954df6c5e96454ecdc12cfebd8283109d22adad9354720d8aaac","durationMs":11160,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,6008],[6008,11160]],"words":[[0,429],[429,1717],[1717,2289],[2289,3004],[3004,3576],[3576,4005],[4005,6008],[6008,6294],[6294,7152],[7152,7438],[7438,8010],[8010,8582],[8582,9440],[9440,9869],[9869,11160]]}}},{"n":2,"text":"It tickles my nose and cracks my lips.\nIt steals the dew from the leaves’ green tips.","sentences":["It tickles my nose and cracks my lips.","It steals the dew from the leaves’ green tips."],"alt":"A child rubs her nose while dew-free leaves hang nearby.","image":{"hash":"sha256:5e8d79b953cbaafda94d8eba67665097021aa022ed7e62eb6d59d63b797b9b0d","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:9019947ac185803b51ca70e3c55706a2bc44b508a9c59e4a26273f668bc60b0a","durationMs":9560,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,4722],[4722,9560]],"words":[[0,230],[230,1036],[1036,1266],[1266,1727],[1727,2073],[2073,2764],[2764,2994],[2994,4722],[4722,4952],[4952,5643],[5643,5989],[5989,6335],[6335,6796],[6796,7142],[7142,7833],[7833,8409],[8409,9560]]}}},{"n":3,"text":"Mama rubs shea butter on my knees,\nand wraps me up against the breeze.","sentences":["Mama rubs shea butter on my knees,\nand wraps me up against the breeze."],"alt":"A mother rubs shea butter on a child’s knees and wraps a cloth around her.","image":{"hash":"sha256:d5fc4ac8fe669634b8ff39d34cb52eb4b6c7b5d44a515379a1b68f8acd34dda6","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:e97936eb46afd7d96625fcf81172f3b4ceff6d725ace9251779c8db90c3de068","durationMs":10240,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,10240]],"words":[[0,621],[621,1242],[1242,1863],[1863,2794],[2794,3104],[3104,3414],[3414,4966],[4966,5431],[5431,6207],[6207,6517],[6517,6827],[6827,7913],[7913,8378],[8378,10240]]}}},{"n":4,"text":"The sun is a coin of orange gold,\na shy little thing, not big or bold.","sentences":["The sun is a coin of orange gold,\na shy little thing, not big or bold."],"alt":"A small orange sun behind a dusty haze.","image":{"hash":"sha256:86ebb8bac6542e42fe0585d84772262c1f1ffd0df26da56965624baaec313406","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:1d8e48b39591f94da3776be2bdd6ede926af0ac87dfdfe58bf6a094f30a105ca","durationMs":10360,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,10360]],"words":[[0,444],[444,888],[888,1184],[1184,1480],[1480,2072],[2072,2368],[2368,3256],[3256,4588],[4588,4884],[4884,5328],[5328,6216],[6216,7696],[7696,8140],[8140,8584],[8584,8880],[8880,10360]]}}},{"n":5,"text":"We fly our kites on the Saturday hill.\nThe wind is a friend that is never still.","sentences":["We fly our kites on the Saturday hill.","The wind is a friend that is never still."],"alt":"Children fly kites on a hill under a hazy sky.","image":{"hash":"sha256:dc595a4a6a21c52a7e4ebc06da60fc0da2c8d583012eaa6bc9361d8de3115896","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:6e85d2fcf1820c065e7447bf8c548e21a487033ae2dc5c50f6d0067a0e221083","durationMs":10320,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,5289],[5289,10320]],"words":[[0,258],[258,645],[645,1032],[1032,1677],[1677,1935],[1935,2322],[2322,3354],[3354,5289],[5289,5676],[5676,6192],[6192,6450],[6450,6708],[6708,7482],[7482,7998],[7998,8256],[8256,8901],[8901,10320]]}}}],"activities":[{"id":"hm-c1","type":"comprehension","afterPage":2,"question":"What does the wind do to the child’s lips?","options":["Cracks them","Paints them blue","Makes them sing"],"correctIndex":0},{"id":"hm-ph","type":"phonics","afterPage":3,"targetSound":"ees","prompt":"Which word rhymes with knees?","options":["breeze","butter","wind"],"correctIndexes":[0]},{"id":"hm-c2","type":"comprehension","afterPage":4,"question":"What is the sun compared to?","options":["A coin of orange gold","A red ball","A white plate"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"This is a metaphor: the poem says the sun is a coin."},{"id":"hm-voc","type":"vocabulary","afterPage":1,"word":"haze","definition":"A thin cloud of dust or smoke in the air that makes things look pale.","distractors":["A kind of bird","A loud noise"]},{"id":"hm-s1","type":"sequencing","prompt":"Put the poem’s pictures in order.","items":["The wind blows across the sky.","Mama rubs shea butter on my knees.","The shy orange sun peeps out.","We fly kites on the hill."]},{"id":"hm-sel","type":"sel","afterPage":5,"prompt":"The poem says the wind is a friend. Do you like harmattan weather?","feelingOptions":["Happy","Cold","Dusty","Playful"]}],"glossary":[{"word":"harmattan","definition":"A dry, dusty wind from the Sahara that blows across West Africa in the dry season.","pages":[1]},{"word":"haze","definition":"A thin cloud of dust that makes the sky look pale.","pages":[1]},{"word":"breeze","definition":"A gentle wind.","pages":[3]},{"word":"kites","definition":"Light toys with a string that fly in the wind.","pages":[5]}],"assets":{"sha256:92644c78c8c2b617a28655a6e6fe362862aa60992b3b5b1a8002cbc5f064a6b9":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/candidates/poem-harmattan-morning/page1-1.webp","bytes":83524,"type":"image/webp"},"sha256:6a85c07447d7954df6c5e96454ecdc12cfebd8283109d22adad9354720d8aaac":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/audio/6a85c07447d7.mp3","bytes":45068,"type":"audio/mpeg"},"sha256:5e8d79b9